.SH NAME
AS860 - Assembles i860\*(tM\fR\fR\fR\fR\& code for the iPSC\*R/860\fR\fR\fR\fR\& system. 
.\" End Summary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
\&\fBas860\fR\fR\& [ \fR\fIoptions\fI\fR\& ] \fR\fIfilename\fI\fR\
\& 
.SH ARGUMENTS 
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fR\fIfilename\fI\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' The name of the i860\& assembly language file. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.LP
You may specify the following \fR\fIoptions\fI\fR\& in any order:
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-o\fR\fR\& \fR\fIobjfile\fI\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Put the output object file in \fR\fI\
objfile\fI\fR\&. If you omit this option, the default object file \
name is produced by stripping any directory prefixes from \fR\fI\
filename\fI\fR\&, stripping any of the suffixes ``.n10'', ``.s'', ``.mac'', or ``.860'', and appending .o. An existing file \
with the same name is silently overwritten.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-l\fR\fR\&[\fR\fIlistfile\fI\fR\&] 	\h'-\w' 'u' Write source listing in the file \fR\fI\
listfile\fI\fR\&, a file in the current working directory. If you \
omit \fR\fIlistfile\fI\fR\&, the listing goes to standard output.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-L\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Preserve text symbols starting with ``.L'' in the debug section.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-R\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Suppress all \fB\&.data\fR\fR\& directives. Code and data are both assembled into the \fB\
\&.text\fR\fR\& section.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-aix\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Force the \fB\&.data\fR\fR\& section to be located at virtual addresses above the \fB\
\&.text\fR\fR\& section. Also changes relocation information for forward-referenced, relocatable symbols.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-intel\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Force the \fB\&.data\fR\fR\& section to be located at virtual addresses above the \fB\
\&.text\fR\fR\& section. Also changes the COFF relocation information to be the Intel-defined format.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-dos\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Does nothing. Accepted for backwards compatibility.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-be\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Process all data defined in \fB\
\&.data\fR\fR\& sections as ``big-endian'' data (high-order byte \
first). Forces the \fB\&-bess\fR\fR\& option, as well.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-bess\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' COFF headers and control structures are written ``big-endian.''
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-elf\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Remove leading underscore from symbols in the output file.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-swapd\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Swap, end-for-end, each 8-byte unit in the \fB\
\&.data\fR\fR\& section of the output file.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-x\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Enable additional checks of the source file to find illegal sequences of \
instructions.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-m\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Ignore the \fB\&.mline\fR\fR\&, \fB\
\&.mfile\fR\fR\&, and \fB\&.mnoline\fR\fR\& assembly directives.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-a\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Do not automatically import symbols that are referenced but otherwise undefined. \
Issues an error message for each occurrence.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-z\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Does nothing. Accepted for backwards compatibility.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-b\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Does nothing. Accepted for backwards compatibility.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-i386\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Put the magic number for Intel386\*(tM\fR\fR\fR\fR\
\& COFF files in the output file, instead of the magic number for i860\
\& COFF files.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-A_step\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Generate workarounds for A-step errata on the \fB\
bc.t\fR\fR\& and \fBbnc.t\fR\fR\& instructions.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-quiet\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Does nothing. Placeholder for future feature(s).
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-qa\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Set COFF timestamp to 0.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
Use \fBas860\fR\fR\& to assemble the named file. 
.LP
You can ensure that the proper options are passed to\fB\& as860\fR\fR\
\& by accessing \fBas860\fR\fR\& using the compiler drivers, \fB\
icc \fR\fRor \fBif77\fR\fR\&.
.LP
Not all illegal sequences are detected when the \fB\&-x\fR\fR\
\& option is used.
.SH SEE ALSO
.LP
\fBar860\fR\fR\&, \fBdump860\fR\fR\&, \fBicc\fR\fR\&, \fBif77\fR\fR\
\&, \fBld860\fR\fR\&, \fBnm860\fR\fR\&, \fBsize860\fR\fR\&, \fB\
strip860\fR\fR\& 
.LP
\fR\fR
.LP
.LP
